## How this project works — driver / worker / store

This project runs on the [GOTM operating protocol](PROTOCOL.md). One discipline underpins everything: **the durable store is the system of record; every working context is disposable and reconstructable from it. Nothing on the hot path is long-lived.**

- **Driver** — the conversation agent. Long-lived but checkpointed: it holds the *plan* (the ledger DAG), the *discipline* (the protocol), and the *human interface* (the ratification ladder). It plans and talks; it never does the work itself. It is the single writer of the store.
- **Worker** — a dispatched subagent. Ephemeral: born fresh for one unit, given only its bounded inputs + its spec, produces exactly one output, returns a terse structured result, and is discarded. All work — however small — is a worker dispatch.
- **Store** — this file-set + the repo. Durable and tiered: a *hot frontier* (active units) and a *cold archive* (closed detail, pulled on demand). Any context can be thrown away and rebuilt from it.

## The file-set

- [`PROTOCOL.md`](PROTOCOL.md) — the operating protocol; the driver reads this on session start
- [`LEDGER.md`](LEDGER.md) — the work DAG + scheduler state, born tiered: a frontier table (ready/active units) and an archive table (closed units)
- [`DECISIONS.md`](DECISIONS.md) — append-only log of ratified decisions
- [`QUESTIONS.md`](QUESTIONS.md) — the ratification parking lot (blocking vs non-blocking)
- [`CONSULTED.md`](CONSULTED.md) — relevant learnings pulled from past projects at start (optional; the *consume* side of the cross-project loop)
- [`LEARNINGS.md`](LEARNINGS.md) — transferable lessons distilled at project end (the *produce* side)
- `audits/` — independent audit outputs (created when audits run)

## How a session starts

1. **Session-start.** On any fresh start (cold restart, `/clear`, or post-compaction), the driver re-hydrates from the store: it reconciles the ledger against disk, rebuilds its working set (active unit + inputs + open questions), and resumes. State lives on disk, never only in chat.
2. **Driver loop.** The driver runs its scheduler over the DAG: read the frontier → compute the ready set → dispatch workers (fan out independent units in parallel) → collect terse results → record status to the store → dispatch fresh audit workers → unblock downstream. Repeat until the DAG drains.

